#!/usr/bin/env bash
# reflex-cadence: 11-59/12 * * * *
# reflex-state: $HOME/.mesh/.interruptibility.state
# reflex-args: --edge
# mesh-interruptibility — CROSS-SENSE FUSION: when may the mesh speak/alert? A coordination primitive
# no single sensor gives. Fuses 8 distinct senses into one INTERRUPTIBILITY band so the mesh (or any
# consumer) can decide "is now an OK time to surface a notification / voice line / board post, or should
# it hold/defer?" — a question none of the inputs answers alone.
#
# WHY THIS FUSION (the gap it fills, audited 2026-07-04):
#   mesh-room-sense      = is someone physically in the room?        (no attention/interrupt info)
#   mesh-operator-focus  = is the NODE under compute load?           (FOCUSED/WORKING/STRESSED/IDLE)
#   mesh-operator-state  = WHERE is the operator (phone-body)?       (AT-PHONE/NEARBY/AWAY/ASLEEP)
#   mesh-room-context    = what is the room's SOCIAL scene?          (ENGAGED-ACTIVE / NIGHT-STILL ...)
#   mesh-activity-tempo  = how ACTIVE is the room (motion)?          (BUSTLE/RESTING/SILENT)
#   mesh-ambient-clock   = are neighbor TVs / appliances on?         (QUIET/ACTIVE/MODERATE)
#   mesh-operator-awake  = is the operator digitally reachable (TG)? (AWAKE/RECENT/IDLE)
#   NONE of them yields the coordination decision "may I interrupt right now?". TYPING alone could be a
#   script; FOCUSED alone could be a runaway job; AWAKE alone could be the operator mid-sentence.
#   Fusing attention (kbd/screen) × occupancy (room) × environment (ambient/tempo/light) × digital
#   presence (operator-awake) × time-of-day yields the band. That cross-domain product is the signal.
#
# Bands (priority order, first match wins; a FRESH STRONG input dominates):
#   DO-NOT-DISTURB — operator demonstrably composing NOW: kbd=TYPING (the one clean hard gate — a
#                    30m-old message or a lit screen alone is attention, not active composition).
#                    Hold non-urgent speaks/alerts.
#   FOCUSED        — operator at desk, screen engaged, present (screen NORMAL/BRIGHT + present).
#   RESTING        — night hours + dark + still + idle + screen off + not digitally active → likely
#                    resting. Defer unless urgent.
#   AVAILABLE      — operator present & idle, room not loud, screen dim/off. OK to interrupt.
#   AWAY           — room genuinely EMPTY (fresh) + no recent digital presence. Batch / defer freely.
#   UNKNOWN        — mixed / unconfirmed signals (e.g. room UNCERTAIN + no digital corroboration).
#                    Visibly distinct from an all-clear so the mesh never assumes "go ahead".
#
# HONEST-DEGRADED CONTRACT (the core rule this fusion exists to honor — empty ≠ failed):
#   An UNREACHABLE input NEVER collapses to a silent all-clear (AVAILABLE/AWAY). The presence/attention
#   axes are LOAD-BEARING for those bands, so if room-sense or kbd-activity is STALE/missing, an
#   AVAILABLE/AWAY result is downgraded to UNKNOWN with the unreachable axis named in `degraded` —
#   visibly different from a genuine AVAILABLE/AWAY whose `degraded` list is empty. A genuine AWAY
#   (room EMPTY, fresh, no digital presence) keeps a clean artifact; an UNREACHABLE room does not.
#   Exit 2 only when EVERY presence/attention axis is unreachable (cannot assess at all).
#
# Usage:
#   mesh-interruptibility            one-line band + signals + reason
#   mesh-interruptibility --edge     emit only on band change (2-consecutive debounce, for cron)
#   mesh-interruptibility --json     machine-readable {band, degraded, signals, reason, ts}
#   mesh-interruptibility --probe    ACTIVE-SENSING: nominate the cheapest disambiguating sense
#   mesh-interruptibility --test     smoke test (synthetic _fuse + _probe assertions, no live sensors)
#
# ── review-efe-epistemic-active-sensing-2026-07-04 (LIVE literature, cross-domain transfer) ───────
# TASK: land on the Free Energy Principle / Active Inference (Friston) from the angle of a DISTRIBUTED
# SENSOR MESH. The mesh has built the PERCEPTION half of AIF exhaustively — precision-weighting
# (mesh-precision), prediction-error/Shannon-surprise (mesh-novelty, incl. epistemic-vs-aleatoric /
# noisy-TV / volatility-scaled bars), Markov-blanket/PEARL (mesh-perimeter), good-regulator
# (mesh-homeostasis), learning-rate (mesh-presence). The ACTION half — "when the posterior is diffuse,
# ACT to reduce the uncertainty" — is the unembodied gap (mesh-presence:192 already flags
# "epistemic-value/active-disambiguation — ACTION-side, which sense to actuate to reduce uncertainty"
# as recognized but NOT built). This lands that primitive.
#
# THE CONCEPT NOT YET EMBODIED: Expected Free Energy (EFE) and ACTIVE SENSING / EPISTEMIC ACTION.
#   G(π) = E_q[ ln q(s|π) − ln p(s,o|π) ]  decomposes into:
#     • epistemic value  = EXPECTED INFORMATION GAIN — how much action π is expected to reduce
#       posterior uncertainty (resolve ambiguity); high when the posterior is diffuse;
#     • pragmatic value  = expected fit to preferred outcomes (instrumental).
#   Active sensing = choose the sensing ACTION that maximises epistemic value per unit cost
#   (saccades are the biological archetype; "a paradigm that will disambiguate ... has high epistemic
#   value → selected when the posterior is diffuse"). Our diffuse-posterior signal is the UNKNOWN band.
#
# LIVE SOURCES (read 2026-07-04, not a fixed list):
#   • Pujol, Sedlak, Salvatori, FRISTON, Dustdar — "Distributed Intelligence in the Computing
#     Continuum with Active Inference", arXiv:2505.24618, 2025. THE cross-domain transfer: a
#     distributed pipeline of IoT sensors + edge services, EACH managed by an AIF agent that minimises
#     EFE; shows AIF agents meet device-aware SLOs from cold start (no MARL training). [the mesh is
#     exactly such a distributed sensor pipeline; each node is an AIF agent candidate.]
#   • "Value of Information and Reward Specification in Active Inference", arXiv:2408.06542, 2024 —
#     the EFE epistemic/pragmatic decomposition and its justifications.
#   • "Active Inference with Dynamic Planning and Information Gain", Entropy 27(8):846 (MDPI), 2025
#     (mdpi.com/1099-4300/27/8/846) — information-gain-driven policy selection.
#   • "Expected Free Energy-based Planning as Variational Inference", arXiv:2504.14898, 2025 —
#     scalable EFE minimisation via message passing.
#
# THE ONE CONCRETE APPLICATION (this edit): `--probe`. On an UNKNOWN/degraded band, nominate the
# single sense whose refresh carries the highest expected information gain per unit COST — a fixed
# rank (kbd > room > awake > screen > tempo > ambient > light) since kbd & room are load-bearing for
# the DND/FOCUSED/AVAILABLE/AWAY bands AND cheap to refresh, while tempo/ambient/light rarely flip a
# band alone. It RECOMMENDS only (never auto-dispatches — conservative-actuator doctrine; an operator
# or a sibling reflex consumes the recommendation). This is epistemic value made operational.
set -uo pipefail
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
[ -n "${HOME:-}" ] || HOME=$(getent passwd "$(id -u)" 2>/dev/null | cut -d: -f6); export HOME

MESH="$HOME/.mesh"
STATE="$MESH/.interruptibility.state"
PENDING="${STATE%.state}.pending"
now="$(date +%s)"

# Staleness budgets = each sense's reflex cadence + grace. --edge reflexes call mesh-state-touch every
# run (mtime = ran-live), so a STATE older than its budget means the reflex genuinely STOPPED, never
# merely "value held" (the conditional-write FALSE-STALE class, fixed mesh-activity-tempo f3f84c1).
KBD_STALE="${MESH_INT_KBD_STALE:-600}"        # mesh-kbd-activity       /5  (3-59/5)  → 10m
SCREEN_STALE="${MESH_INT_SCREEN_STALE:-700}"  # mesh-screen-state       /9  (2-59/9)  → ~12m
ROOM_STALE="${MESH_INT_ROOM_STALE:-1200}"     # mesh-room-sense         /15 (2-59/15) → 20m
AMBIENT_STALE="${MESH_INT_AMBIENT_STALE:-2100}" # mesh-ambient-clock    /30 (6-59/30) → 35m
TEMPO_STALE="${MESH_INT_TEMPO_STALE:-2100}"   # mesh-activity-tempo     /10 (8-59/10) → 35m (change-gated)
LIGHT_STALE="${MESH_INT_LIGHT_STALE:-2100}"   # mesh-light              /30 (9-59/30) → 35m

# read_axis <file> <stale_limit_s> → echoes "<VERDICT>|<age>" or "UNREACHABLE|<age>(stale)" or "UNREACHABLE|-"
# A missing/empty file is UNREACHABLE (sense never ran / organ absent); a stale file is UNREACHABLE(stale).
# Crucially a REAL reading — even a "negative" one like IDLE / EMPTY / SILENCE — is returned as-is: a
# genuine empty is NOT the same as an unreachable sense, and this helper keeps them distinct by construction.
# Takes the first whitespace-delimited token of field 1 (verdicts are single tokens; some state files
# append prose like light-state's "OFFLINE <ts>" — `tr -d` would MUNGE that into "OFFLINE<ts>").
read_axis() {
  local f="$1" lim="$2" m age v
  [ -f "$f" ] && [ -s "$f" ] || { echo "UNREACHABLE|-"; return; }
  m="$(stat -c %Y "$f" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"; [ "$m" -gt 0 ] || { echo "UNREACHABLE|-"; return; }
  age=$(( now - m ))
  v="$(head -1 "$f" 2>/dev/null | cut -d'|' -f1 | awk '{print $1}')"
  [ -n "$v" ] || { echo "UNREACHABLE|${age}s"; return; }
  if [ "$age" -gt "$lim" ]; then echo "UNREACHABLE|${age}s(stale)"; else echo "$v|${age}s"; fi
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORGAN ABSENCE — "this node HAS NO SUCH ORGAN" is not "the sense broke".
#
# read_axis above cannot tell them apart by construction: a missing artifact reads UNREACHABLE
# whether the reflex DIED yesterday or the organ never existed on this body. That collapse (the
# collapsed-reason class — blind and quiet rendered identical) did not merely mislabel this tool,
# it turned it into a CONSTANT. Measured 2026-08-20 by sweeping _fuse itself: with kbd and screen
# both UNREACHABLE, all 16800 combinations of the remaining six axes (room × ambient × tempo ×
# light × awake × hour) return UNKNOWN — 16800 of 16800. Every band the ladder can reach is gated
# on a real kbd or screen read, and the honest-degraded override then takes AWAY as well, so the
# ONE band left is the fallback. The control arm is the proof it is the absence and not the ladder:
# the identical sweep with kbd=IDLE screen=OFF reaches AVAILABLE(2880) AWAY(2340) RESTING(960),
# i.e. 4 bands and 37% non-UNKNOWN. mesh-home has no keyboard at all and no screen session, so 240
# consecutive runs published the same word and reflex-health could only report it as a value-frozen
# label — the sense was dead in a way that reads exactly like a stable world.
#
# The honest-degraded override that causes it is RIGHT for a broken axis (never a silent all-clear
# on a dead sense) and WRONG for an absent one: an organ that cannot exist is not coming back, so
# withholding forever buys no safety, it just deletes the sense. So absence gets its own token and
# its own field on the wire — an all-clear built on a narrower axis set is published WITH that set
# named (`n/a=kbd,screen`), never silently upgraded to a full-evidence one.
#
# The oracle is the organ's OWN `--test` rc=2 — the mesh's honest-n/a contract, the same one
# mesh-reflex-health's organ-absence clause uses — and it carries that clause's TEST-FORGERY refusal
# with it: a `--test` that CREATES the artifact is not evidence of absence, it is evidence the test
# writes the record it exists to check, so the verdict is FORGED and the axis stays UNREACHABLE.
# A tool that is not on PATH is UNPROBEABLE, never ABSENT — "could not ask" is not "the organ is
# gone" (the same distinction reflex-health gate G asserts).
#
# _absent_verdict <tool_on_path 0|1> <artifact_before 0|1> <test_rc> <artifact_after 0|1>
#   → ABSENT | PRESENT | UNPROBEABLE | FORGED.  Pure, offline-testable.
_absent_verdict() {
  local onpath="$1" before="$2" rc="$3" after="$4"
  [ "$onpath" = 1 ]  || { printf 'UNPROBEABLE'; return; }
  [ "$before" = 0 ]  || { printf 'PRESENT';     return; }   # a corpse artifact is not an absent organ
  [ "$rc" = 2 ]      || { printf 'PRESENT';     return; }   # rc 0/1 = it can produce; nothing absent
  [ "$after" = 0 ]   || { printf 'FORGED';      return; }   # the dry-run wrote the artifact — refuse
  printf 'ABSENT'
}

# organ_absent <tool> <artifact> → rc 0 when the organ is structurally ABSENT on this node.
# Cached: `--test` is the expensive part and absence is a property of the BODY, not of the minute.
# The cache is keyed by tool and carries its own stamp; a miss re-probes, a hit costs a read.
ORGAN_CACHE="${MESH_INT_ORGAN_CACHE:-$MESH/.interruptibility.organs}"
ORGAN_TTL="${MESH_INT_ORGAN_TTL:-21600}"          # 6h — an organ does not appear between cron ticks
organ_absent() {
  local tool="$1" art="$2" line v stamp now2 before rc after
  now2="$(date +%s)"
  if [ -f "$ORGAN_CACHE" ]; then
    line="$(grep -m1 "^${tool} " "$ORGAN_CACHE" 2>/dev/null || true)"
    if [ -n "$line" ]; then
      v="$(printf '%s' "$line" | awk '{print $2}')"; stamp="$(printf '%s' "$line" | awk '{print $3}')"
      case "$stamp" in ''|*[!0-9]*) stamp=0 ;; esac
      if [ $((now2 - stamp)) -lt "$ORGAN_TTL" ]; then
        [ "$v" = ABSENT ] && return 0 || return 1
      fi
    fi
  fi
  command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1 && local onpath=1 || local onpath=0
  [ -f "$art" ] && [ -s "$art" ] && before=1 || before=0
  rc=9
  [ "$onpath" = 1 ] && [ "$before" = 0 ] && { timeout 90 "$tool" --test >/dev/null 2>&1; rc=$?; }
  [ -f "$art" ] && [ -s "$art" ] && after=1 || after=0
  v="$(_absent_verdict "$onpath" "$before" "$rc" "$after")"
  # rewrite the row atomically-enough (single line, single writer per tool name)
  { [ -f "$ORGAN_CACHE" ] && grep -v "^${tool} " "$ORGAN_CACHE" 2>/dev/null || true
    printf '%s %s %s\n' "$tool" "$v" "$now2"; } > "${ORGAN_CACHE}.tmp" 2>/dev/null \
    && mv -f "${ORGAN_CACHE}.tmp" "$ORGAN_CACHE" 2>/dev/null || true
  [ "$v" = ABSENT ] && return 0 || return 1
}

# light_vocab <token> → the token itself if it is a real mesh-light level, else UNREACHABLE.
# Pure so --test can drive it; the live path below calls THIS, never an inline copy of the case
# (an inline copy is unreachable from the test block, which is exactly how the TWILIGHT band went
# uncaught for 47 days — see the vocab-coverage gate).
light_vocab() {
  case "$1" in DARK|DIM|TWILIGHT|MODERATE|LIT|BRIGHT) printf '%s' "$1" ;; *) printf 'UNREACHABLE' ;; esac
}

# _fuse <kbd> <screen> <room> <ambient> <tempo> <light> <op_awake> <hour>
# Sets globals: band, reason, degraded, absent, signals. Pure, offline-testable (no I/O).
# Each axis is either a real verdict or the literal token "UNREACHABLE".
_fuse() {
  local kbd="$1" scr="$2" room="$3" amb="$4" tmp="$5" lt="$6" oa="$7" hr="$8"
  local night quiet_audio still dark
  band="UNKNOWN"; reason=""; degraded=""; absent=""
  local deg=() na=()
  # DEGRADED = a sense that should be producing and is not (dead/stale) — the organ IS the fix.
  # ABSENT   = a sense this body does not have (its own --test exits 2) — nothing to fix, ever.
  # They are kept in SEPARATE lists because they license opposite things downstream: a degraded axis
  # withholds an all-clear (it may come back and contradict it), an absent one narrows the basis the
  # all-clear is built on and says so. Collapsing them is what made this tool a constant.
  [ "$kbd"  = ABSENT ]      && na+=("kbd")
  [ "$scr"  = ABSENT ]      && na+=("screen")
  [ "$room" = ABSENT ]      && na+=("room")
  [ "$amb"  = ABSENT ]      && na+=("ambient")
  [ "$tmp"  = ABSENT ]      && na+=("tempo")
  [ "$lt"   = ABSENT ]      && na+=("light")
  [ "$kbd"  = UNREACHABLE ] && deg+=("kbd-unreachable")
  [ "$scr"  = UNREACHABLE ] && deg+=("screen-unreachable")
  [ "$room" = UNREACHABLE ] && deg+=("room-unreachable")
  [ "$amb"  = UNREACHABLE ] && deg+=("ambient-unreachable")
  [ "$tmp"  = UNREACHABLE ] && deg+=("tempo-unreachable")
  [ "$lt"   = UNREACHABLE ] && deg+=("light-unreachable")
  [ "$oa"   = UNKNOWN ]     && deg+=("op-awake-unknown")
  if [ "${#deg[@]}" -gt 0 ]; then local IFS=,; degraded="${deg[*]}"; fi
  if [ "${#na[@]}"  -gt 0 ]; then local IFS=,; absent="${na[*]}"; fi

  # Predicates (UNREACHABLE axes are conservative: not night-gating on a missing clock, etc.)
  [ "$hr" -ge 22 ] 2>/dev/null || [ "$hr" -le 6 ] 2>/dev/null && night=1 || night=0
  case "$amb" in QUIET|SILENT) quiet_audio=1;; *) quiet_audio=0;; esac
  case "$tmp" in SILENT|RESTING|STILL) still=1;; *) still=0;; esac
  case "$lt"  in DARK|DIM) dark=1;; *) dark=0;; esac  # TWILIGHT/MODERATE+ = some light → dark=0

  local present=0
  { [ "$room" = PRESENT ] || [ "$oa" = AWAKE ] || [ "$oa" = RECENT ]; } && present=1

  # 1. DO-NOT-DISTURB: operator actively composing (fresh TYPING is the one clean hard gate — a recent
  #    message or a lit screen is attention, not active composition).
  if [ "$kbd" = TYPING ]; then
    band="DO-NOT-DISTURB"; reason="keyboard TYPING — operator composing"
  # 2. FOCUSED: at desk, screen engaged, operator present.
  elif { [ "$scr" = NORMAL ] || [ "$scr" = BRIGHT ]; } && [ "$present" = 1 ]; then
    band="FOCUSED"; reason="screen engaged + operator present (room=$room awake=$oa)"
  # 3. RESTING: night + dark + still + idle + screen off/dim + not digitally active.
  elif [ "$night" = 1 ] && [ "$dark" = 1 ] && [ "$still" = 1 ] \
       && { [ "$kbd" = IDLE ] || [ "$kbd" = LIGHT ] || [ "$kbd" = ABSENT ]; } \
       && { [ "$scr" = OFF ] || [ "$scr" = DIM ] || [ "$scr" = UNREACHABLE ] || [ "$scr" = ABSENT ]; } \
       && [ "$oa" != AWAKE ]; then
    band="RESTING"; reason="night + dark + still + idle — likely resting"
  # 4. AVAILABLE: operator present & idle, room not loud. kbd must be a real read OR structurally
  #    ABSENT — never merely UNREACHABLE. The two are different claims: an unreachable kbd may come
  #    back TYPING and contradict this line, an absent one cannot, so the all-clear rests on the
  #    narrower basis and publishes it (`n/a=kbd`) instead of being withheld forever.
  elif [ "$present" = 1 ] && { [ "$kbd" = IDLE ] || [ "$kbd" = LIGHT ] || [ "$kbd" = ABSENT ]; } \
       && [ "$quiet_audio" = 1 ] && [ "$kbd" != UNREACHABLE ]; then
    band="AVAILABLE"; reason="operator present, idle, room not loud (room=$room awake=$oa)"
  # 5. AWAY: room genuinely EMPTY (fresh) + no recent digital presence.
  elif [ "$room" = EMPTY ] && [ "$oa" != AWAKE ] && [ "$oa" != RECENT ]; then
    band="AWAY"; reason="room empty + no recent digital presence"
  # 6. fallback.
  else
    band="UNKNOWN"; reason="mixed/unconfirmed signals (kbd=$kbd screen=$scr room=$room tempo=$tmp light=$lt awake=$oa)"
  fi

  # HONEST-DEGRADED OVERRIDE (the no-silent-all-clear rule): an AVAILABLE/AWAY all-clear built on an
  # UNREACHABLE load-bearing axis is downgraded to UNKNOWN with the axis named in `degraded`. A genuine
  # all-clear (fresh axes) is untouched — its degraded list is empty, so the two artifacts differ visibly.
  # This is the explicit guard even though the branches above already gate on real reads: it locks the
  # contract against future logic drift and makes the rule falsifiable in --test.
  if [ "$band" = AVAILABLE ] || [ "$band" = AWAY ]; then
    # UNREACHABLE only — an ABSENT axis is deliberately NOT a trigger here. Downgrading on absence
    # is what pinned this node at UNKNOWN for 240 runs: the withheld all-clear could never be
    # un-withheld, because the organ it was waiting on does not exist on this body.
    local _wh=""
    [ "$room" = UNREACHABLE ] && _wh="room"
    [ "$kbd"  = UNREACHABLE ] && _wh="${_wh:+$_wh }kbd"
    if [ -n "$_wh" ]; then
      band="UNKNOWN"
      reason="withheld all-clear: ${_wh} unreachable — ${reason}"
    fi
  fi

  signals="kbd=${kbd} screen=${scr} room=${room} ambient=${amb} tempo=${tmp} light=${lt} awake=${oa} hour=${hr} night=${night}${absent:+ n/a=${absent}}"
}

# Exit-code policy: exit 2 only when EVERY presence/attention axis is dark (cannot assess at all).
# A single reachable axis is enough to produce an honest (if coarse) band.
# An ABSENT axis is dark too: it carries no information about the operator, it merely carries a
# REASON. "cannot assess at all" must not become false just because the reason for one axis got
# more precise — that would be the mirror of the collapse this file fixes.
_dark_axis() { case "$1" in UNREACHABLE|ABSENT) return 0 ;; *) return 1 ;; esac; }
_all_dark() {
  _dark_axis "$1" || return 1
  _dark_axis "$2" || return 1
  _dark_axis "$3" || return 1
  [ "$7" = UNKNOWN ] || return 1
  return 0
}

# _probe <kbd> <screen> <room> <ambient> <tempo> <light> <op_awake>
# Sets globals: probe_sense, probe_cmd, probe_reason. Pure, offline-testable (no I/O).
# THE ACTIVE-SENSING / EPISTEMIC-ACTION PRIMITIVE (review-efe-epistemic-active-sensing-2026-07-04):
# when the fused band is UNKNOWN (posterior diffuse) because an axis is degraded/unreachable, the
# perception half is done — active inference's ACTION half says: ACT to reduce the uncertainty. This
# nominates the single sense whose refresh carries the highest EXPECTED INFORMATION GAIN per unit
# COST (the EFE epistemic-value term). RECOMMENDS only (never auto-dispatches). Rank is fixed =
# (info-gain for the band × cheapness): kbd & room are load-bearing for DND/FOCUSED/AVAILABLE/AWAY
# and cheap → top; awake/screen next; tempo/ambient/light rarely flip a band alone → bottom.
_probe() {
  local kbd="$1" scr="$2" room="$3" amb="$4" tmp="$5" lt="$6" oa="$7"
  probe_sense="none"; probe_cmd=""; probe_reason=""; probe_gamma=""; probe_gamma_reason=""
  [ "$kbd"  = UNREACHABLE ] && local need_kbd=1  || local need_kbd=0
  [ "$room" = UNREACHABLE ] && local need_room=1 || local need_room=0
  [ "$oa"   = UNKNOWN ]     && local need_awake=1 || local need_awake=0
  [ "$scr"  = UNREACHABLE ] && local need_scr=1  || local need_scr=0
  [ "$tmp"  = UNREACHABLE ] && local need_tmp=1  || local need_tmp=0
  [ "$amb"  = UNREACHABLE ] && local need_amb=1  || local need_amb=0
  [ "$lt"   = UNREACHABLE ] && local need_lt=1   || local need_lt=0
  # nothing degraded → no epistemic action (band confident even if UNKNOWN via MIXED real signals —
  # a refresh would not help; that case is reported honestly, never fabricated as "probe something").
  [ $((need_kbd+need_room+need_awake+need_scr+need_tmp+need_amb+need_lt)) -eq 0 ] && return
  # γ — EXPECTED PRECISION OVER POLICIES (review-efe-gamma-probe-confidence-2026-07-29): _probe below is
  # an argmax over a FIXED epistemic-action ranking — it names the top probe but not how ALONE it stands.
  # Friston et al. 2015 ("Active inference and epistemic value") carry a precision γ ON the policy
  # selection = CONFIDENCE that the chosen action is decisive; Hesp et al. 2021 ("Deeply Felt Affect")
  # read that confidence as valence. The peakedness of the probe distribution is that γ: resolving ONE
  # axis collapses the band only when the posterior is diffuse along that ONE axis. Count the diffuse
  # LOAD-BEARING axes (kbd/room/awake/screen — the tier that can flip a band; tempo/ambient/light are
  # weak levers that "rarely flip a band alone"). One load-bearing axis diffuse → the probe is decisive
  # (γ HIGH); many diffuse, or only weak levers → the single refresh is a PARTIAL move (γ LOW).
  local lb_deg=$((need_kbd+need_room+need_awake+need_scr))
  # priority order: sense | cheapest refresh cmd | why a refresh would disambiguate the band
  local entry name rest cmd why
  for entry in \
    "kbd|mesh-kbd-activity|refresh distinguishes DO-NOT-DISTURB vs AVAILABLE (TYPING vs IDLE)" \
    "room|mesh-room-sense|refresh resolves PRESENT/EMPTY — load-bearing for AVAILABLE vs AWAY" \
    "awake|mesh-operator-awake|refresh confirms digital presence — load-bearing for AWAY" \
    "screen|mesh-screen-state|refresh resolves screen-engaged (FOCUSED) vs off" \
    "tempo|mesh-activity-tempo|refresh confirms still-vs-bustle (RESTING gating)" \
    "ambient|mesh-ambient-clock|refresh confirms quiet-vs-loud (AVAILABLE gating)" \
    "light|mesh-light|refresh confirms dark-vs-lit (RESTING/night gating)"; do
    name="${entry%%|*}"; rest="${entry#*|}"; cmd="${rest%%|*}"; why="${rest#*|}"
    case "$name" in
      kbd)     [ "$need_kbd"  = 1 ] || continue ;;
      room)    [ "$need_room" = 1 ] || continue ;;
      awake)   [ "$need_awake" = 1 ] || continue ;;
      screen)  [ "$need_scr"  = 1 ] || continue ;;
      tempo)   [ "$need_tmp"  = 1 ] || continue ;;
      ambient) [ "$need_amb"  = 1 ] || continue ;;
      light)   [ "$need_lt"   = 1 ] || continue ;;
    esac
    probe_sense="$name"; probe_cmd="$cmd"; probe_reason="$why"
    case "$name" in kbd|room|awake|screen) local nom_lb=1 ;; *) local nom_lb=0 ;; esac
    if [ "$nom_lb" = 1 ] && [ "$lb_deg" -eq 1 ]; then
      probe_gamma=HIGH
      probe_gamma_reason="decisive — the ONLY load-bearing axis diffuse; resolving it collapses the band"
    elif [ "$lb_deg" -ge 2 ]; then
      probe_gamma=LOW
      probe_gamma_reason="$lb_deg load-bearing axes diffuse — one refresh is a PARTIAL move (band won't fully collapse; batch-probe or wait, don't treat as a fix)"
    else
      probe_gamma=LOW
      probe_gamma_reason="only weak-lever axes diffuse — a refresh rarely flips the band alone (low expected precision-gain)"
    fi
    return
  done
}

# _foreclosure <form|raw> [rev exc att] [+party [brev bexc batt]]
# Sets globals: fc_score fc_band fc_rev fc_exc fc_att fc_bscore fc_agg fc_caveat fc_reason. Pure,
# offline-testable.
# THE ASSISTIVE-EMPOWERMENT AXIS (review-info-theory-agency-assistive-operator-empowerment-2026-07-28):
# the band above answers "may I interrupt NOW?" — a TIMING question over the operator's attention. It
# does NOT answer the ORTHOGONAL question "which FORM of the act least FORECLOSES the operator's own
# option-space?". Myers, Ellis, Levine, Eysenbach & Dragan, "Learning to Assist Humans WITHOUT
# Inferring Rewards" (NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2411.02623) argue an assistant should MAXIMIZE THE HUMAN'S
# EMPOWERMENT — the mutual information between the human's actions and future states, i.e. keep his
# reachable-future set as large as possible — INSTEAD of inferring his reward and driving to it (their
# ESR objective). Two proactive acts carrying the SAME intent are NOT equal at the same band: a
# dismissible private line preserves the operator's control; seizing the one shared speaker, or acting
# toward a third party on his behalf, forecloses it. This scores that foreclosure so a consumer can
# prefer the MIN-foreclosure form of its intent. Report-only — nominates, never actuates.
#   foreclosure = reversibility + exclusivity + attention-capture   (each 0..3; total 0..9)
#     reversibility   — can he undo/ignore it at ~zero cost?   (0=ignore, 3=irreversible)
#     exclusivity     — does it seize a shared/scarce resource he then loses? (0=private, 3=scarce-external)
#     attention       — does it commandeer his attention (forced context switch)? (0=pull, 3=hard capture)
#
# THE BYSTANDER IS A PARTY, NOT A CAVEAT (review-info-theory-agency-fair-power-aggregation-softmin-interruptibility-2026-08-20):
# until 2026-08-20 a co-present third party entered this score as a STRING (`fc_caveat`) that never
# touched `fc_score` or `fc_band` — a safety knob named in prose. The comment even asserted the score
# was "net-across-parties", i.e. a SUM, which it neither computed nor should: Heitzig & Potham,
# "A Fair Objective for Human-Empowerment-Preserving AI" (arXiv:2608.08240, 8 Aug 2026) derive from
# axioms that the utilitarian SUM is the WRONG aggregator over several humans' power — it permits
# unlimited compensation, so one party's collapse is paid for by another's gain (the utility-monster
# problem) — and so are the Nash product (loses Pigou–Dalton) and hard leximin (too extreme). Their
# aggregate is the inequality-averse soft-min
#       P(s) = -log2 SUM_h 2^(-xi * I_h(s))        (xi > 0 = inequality aversion)
# We port it verbatim on our finite scale, with I_h = MAXF - f_h ("residual option-bits left to h")
# and P normalised by xi so it stays in bit units (xi -> inf gives the exact min):
#       fc_agg = MAXF - ( -log2 SUM_h 2^(-xi*I_h) ) / xi
# Two of their axioms are the load-bearing ones here and BOTH are asserted in --test:
#   * DISEMPOWERMENT FOCUS — a party the act does not touch (f_h = 0) is all-powerful with respect to
#     it and is EXCLUDED from the sum, so its presence cannot change the verdict. This is what makes
#     the single-party path reduce EXACTLY to the old number (no regression), and it is why an
#     unaffected bystander does not silently tax every score.
#   * LIMITED TRADE-OFF (their Cor. 4.1) — no amount of operator empowerment buys a bystander's
#     foreclosure back. An act that is FREE for the operator and irreversible for a bystander bands
#     HIGH, where the old code banded it LOW with a footnote.
# Report-only, like everything else here: it nominates the min-foreclosure form, it never actuates.
# Bystander dims per form are the SAME three axes read from the third party's seat — a bystander
# typically has WORSE reversibility (they cannot dismiss a line addressed to someone else) and the
# same exclusivity (they lose the same shared speaker/TV), while gaining none of the intent.
_foreclosure() {
  local form="${1:-}"
  fc_score=""; fc_band=""; fc_rev=""; fc_exc=""; fc_att=""; fc_caveat=""; fc_reason=""
  fc_bscore=""; fc_agg=""
  local rev="" exc="" att="" party="" desc="" brev="" bexc="" batt=""
  #                                          rev exc att | bystander: brev bexc batt
  case "$form" in
    tg-line)          rev=0 exc=0 att=0 brev=0 bexc=0 batt=0 party="${2:-}" desc="dismissible private TG text — read/ignore at will" ;;
    board-post)       rev=0 exc=0 att=0 brev=0 bexc=0 batt=0 party="${2:-}" desc="board/chat line — pull, operator reads on his own terms" ;;
    ambient-mix)      rev=1 exc=2 att=1 brev=2 bexc=2 batt=1 party="${2:-}" desc="quiet mix on the shared speaker — occupies the one audio channel" ;;
    speaker-say)      rev=1 exc=2 att=2 brev=2 bexc=2 batt=2 party="${2:-}" desc="voice line on the shared speaker — seizes audio + attention" ;;
    speaker-autoplay) rev=2 exc=2 att=2 brev=3 bexc=2 batt=2 party="${2:-}" desc="auto-played audio — he must actively stop it" ;;
    ring-call)        rev=2 exc=1 att=2 brev=1 bexc=0 batt=2 party="${2:-}" desc="phone ring/call — hard attention capture, must dismiss" ;;
    tv-seize)         rev=2 exc=3 att=2 brev=3 bexc=3 batt=2 party="${2:-}" desc="takes over the shared TV — removes his own access" ;;
    act-third-party)  rev=3 exc=3 att=1 brev=3 bexc=3 batt=3 party="${2:-}" desc="acts toward a 3rd party for him — irreversible, commits his standing" ;;
    raw)              rev="${2:-}" exc="${3:-}" att="${4:-}" party="${5:-}"
                      brev="${6:-0}" bexc="${7:-0}" batt="${8:-0}" desc="raw form" ;;
    *)  fc_reason="unknown action form '$form' — refusing to score (an unscored form is NOT maximally empowering)"; return 1 ;;
  esac
  if [ -z "$rev" ] || [ -z "$exc" ] || [ -z "$att" ]; then
    fc_reason="foreclosure dims missing (raw needs <rev> <exc> <att>, each 0..3)"; return 1; fi
  case "$rev$exc$att" in *[!0-3]*) fc_reason="foreclosure dims must each be 0..3 (got rev=$rev exc=$exc att=$att)"; return 1 ;; esac
  case "$brev$bexc$batt" in *[!0-3]*) fc_reason="bystander dims must each be 0..3 (got brev=$brev bexc=$bexc batt=$batt)"; return 1 ;; esac
  fc_rev=$rev; fc_exc=$exc; fc_att=$att; fc_score=$((rev+exc+att))
  fc_reason="$desc"

  # MULTI-PARTY aggregation. Without a co-present party the aggregate IS the operator's own score
  # (Disempowerment Focus, degenerate case) — the old number, bit for bit.
  local bs="" agg="$fc_score"
  case "$party" in
    +party|party|multi)
      bs=$((brev+bexc+batt)); fc_bscore=$bs
      agg="$(_fc_aggregate "$fc_score" "$bs")"
      fc_caveat="multi-party: bystander-foreclosure=${bs}/9 folded in — aggregate=${agg}/9 by inequality-averse soft-min (xi=${MESH_FC_XI:-1}), NOT a sum: the operator's empowerment cannot buy it back"
      ;;
  esac
  fc_agg="$agg"
  fc_band="$(_fc_band "$agg")"
  return 0
}

# _fc_aggregate <f_operator> <f_bystander> … → aggregate foreclosure on the 0..9 scale, 1 decimal.
# Heitzig & Potham's P(s) = -log2 SUM_h 2^(-xi*I_h), I_h = 9 - f_h, normalised by xi and re-expressed
# as foreclosure. Parties with f_h = 0 are untouched by the act → excluded (Disempowerment Focus).
_fc_aggregate() {
  awk -v xi="${MESH_FC_XI:-1}" -v maxf=9 'BEGIN{
    if (xi <= 0) xi = 1
    s = 0; n = 0
    for (i = 1; i < ARGC; i++) { f = ARGV[i] + 0; if (f <= 0) continue; I = maxf - f; s += 2 ^ (-xi * I); n++ }
    if (n == 0) { print "0.0"; exit }          # nobody foreclosed by this act
    P = -log(s) / log(2) / xi                  # aggregate residual option-bits (soft-min over parties)
    F = maxf - P
    if (F < 0) F = 0; if (F > maxf) F = maxf
    printf "%.1f\n", F
  }' "$@"
}

# _fc_band <aggregate> → LOW|MED|HIGH (same cut points the single-party score always used)
_fc_band() {
  awk -v f="${1:-0}" 'BEGIN{ if (f <= 2) print "LOW"; else if (f <= 5) print "MED"; else print "HIGH" }'
}

if [ "${1:-}" = --foreclosure ]; then
  shift
  [ $# -ge 1 ] || { echo "usage: mesh-interruptibility --foreclosure <form> [+party]  |  --foreclosure raw <rev> <exc> <att> [+party [<brev> <bexc> <batt>]]" >&2
    echo "  forms: tg-line board-post ambient-mix speaker-say speaker-autoplay ring-call tv-seize act-third-party" >&2
    echo "  +party folds a co-present BYSTANDER in by inequality-averse soft-min (MESH_FC_XI, default 1) — never a sum" >&2; exit 2; }
  label="$1"
  if _foreclosure "$@"; then
    cav=""; [ -n "$fc_caveat" ] && cav=" caveat=$fc_caveat"
    par=""; [ -n "$fc_bscore" ] && par=" bystander=$fc_bscore/9 aggregate=$fc_agg/9"
    printf '[interruptibility:foreclosure] %s foreclosure=%d/9 band=%s (rev=%d exc=%d att=%d)%s — %s%s\n' \
      "$label" "$fc_score" "$fc_band" "$fc_rev" "$fc_exc" "$fc_att" "$par" "$fc_reason" "$cav"
    exit 0
  else
    echo "[interruptibility:foreclosure] $fc_reason" >&2; exit 2
  fi
fi

if [ "${1:-}" = --test ]; then
  _t() {  # _t <desc> <expect_band> <args...>
    local desc="$1" exp="$2"; shift 2
    _fuse "$@"; [ "$band" = "$exp" ] || { echo "  FAIL: $desc → expected $exp, got $band ($reason)"; exit 1; }
  }
  # 1. TYPING → DO-NOT-DISTURB (dominates everything)
  _t "kbd TYPING → DND" DO-NOT-DISTURB  TYPING OFF    EMPTY    QUIET  SILENT DARK  IDLE  14
  # 1b. digitally active + screen engaged → FOCUSED (a recent message is attention, not active composition)
  _t "awake+BRIGHT → FOCUSED" FOCUSED   IDLE  BRIGHT  PRESENT  QUIET  RESTING LIT AWAKE 14
  # 2. screen engaged + present → FOCUSED
  _t "NORMAL+present → FOCUSED" FOCUSED   LIGHT NORMAL  PRESENT  ACTIVE BUSTLE LIT AWAKE 14
  # 3. RESTING: night + dark + still + idle + screen off + not awake
  _t "night-dark-still-idle → RESTING" RESTING IDLE OFF PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE 2
  # 3b. not night → not RESTING (falls through; present+idle+quiet → AVAILABLE)
  _t "daytime dark-still → AVAILABLE" AVAILABLE IDLE OFF PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE 14
  # 4. AVAILABLE: present + idle + quiet
  _t "present-idle-quiet → AVAILABLE" AVAILABLE IDLE DIM PRESENT QUIET RESTING LIT IDLE 14
  # 4b. loud ambient → not AVAILABLE (falls to UNKNOWN, no DND/FOCUSED/RESTING match)
  _t "present-idle-LOUD → UNKNOWN" UNKNOWN IDLE DIM PRESENT ACTIVE RESTING LIT IDLE 14
  # 5. AWAY: room EMPTY + no digital presence
  _t "room EMPTY → AWAY" AWAY       IDLE OFF    EMPTY    QUIET  SILENT DARK IDLE 14
  # 5b. room EMPTY but digitally AWAKE → NOT AWAY (present via digital) → AVAILABLE
  _t "EMPTY+AWAKE → AVAILABLE" AVAILABLE IDLE OFF EMPTY QUIET SILENT DARK AWAKE 14
  # 6. HONEST-DEGRADED (the core contract): room UNREACHABLE must NOT yield AWAY/AVAILABLE all-clear.
  _t "room UNREACHABLE ≠ AWAY" UNKNOWN IDLE OFF UNREACHABLE QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE 14
  _t "room UNREACHABLE ≠ AVAILABLE(1)" UNKNOWN IDLE DIM UNREACHABLE QUIET RESTING LIT AWAKE 14
  # 6b. kbd UNREACHABLE must NOT yield an AVAILABLE all-clear (withheld).
  _t "kbd UNREACHABLE ≠ AVAILABLE" UNKNOWN UNREACHABLE DIM PRESENT QUIET RESTING LIT IDLE 14
  # 6c. a genuine AWAY keeps a CLEAN (empty) degraded list; an UNREACHABLE-room verdict does not.
  _fuse IDLE OFF EMPTY QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE 14
  [ -z "$degraded" ] || { echo "  FAIL: genuine AWAY must have empty degraded (got '$degraded')"; exit 1; }
  _fuse IDLE OFF UNREACHABLE QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE 14
  printf '%s' "$degraded" | grep -q 'room-unreachable' || { echo "  FAIL: unreachable room must list room-unreachable (got '$degraded')"; exit 1; }
  # 6d. visibly distinct artifacts: AWAY vs the withheld-UNKNOWN carry different band AND degraded.
  _fuse IDLE OFF EMPTY QUIET SILENCE DARK IDLE 14; _b1="$band"; _d1="$degraded"
  _fuse IDLE OFF UNREACHABLE QUIET SILENCE DARK IDLE 14; _b2="$band"; _d2="$degraded"
  [ "$_b1" != "$_b2" ] || { echo "  FAIL: AWAY vs unreachable must differ in band"; exit 1; }
  [ "$_d1" != "$_d2" ] || { echo "  FAIL: AWAY vs unreachable must differ in degraded"; exit 1; }
  # 7. exit-code policy: all presence/attention dark → _all_dark returns 0
  _all_dark UNREACHABLE UNREACHABLE UNREACHABLE QUIET SILENT DARK UNKNOWN || { echo "  FAIL: all-dark should assess-unable"; exit 1; }
  _all_dark IDLE OFF PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK AWAKE && { echo "  FAIL: reachable axes should not be all-dark"; exit 1; }
  # 7b. THE REAL PATH, not just the predicate: drive the whole script with every axis dark and assert
  # it exits 2 (honest cannot-assess). Calling _all_dark directly here is what let the 4-arg call site
  # at the bottom die on `$7: unbound variable` for a day while this test stayed green — an in-process
  # call proves the predicate, never the call site. Empty HOME => MESH has no state files (all axes
  # UNREACHABLE) and mesh-operator-awake is off PATH (awake=UNKNOWN).
  _ad="$(mktemp -d)"
  _out="$(env -i HOME="$_ad" PATH=/usr/bin:/bin bash "$0" 2>&1)"; _rc=$?
  rm -rf "$_ad"
  [ "$_rc" = 2 ] || { echo "  FAIL: all-dark real run must exit 2, got rc=$_rc: $_out"; exit 1; }
  printf '%s' "$_out" | grep -q 'cannot assess' || { echo "  FAIL: all-dark real run must say cannot assess (got '$_out')"; exit 1; }
  # 8. night boundary
  _hr=23; { [ "$_hr" -ge 22 ] || [ "$_hr" -le 6 ]; } || { echo "  FAIL: 23h should be night"; exit 1; }
  _hr=7;  { [ "$_hr" -ge 22 ] || [ "$_hr" -le 6 ]; } && { echo "  FAIL: 7h should NOT be night"; exit 1; }

  # read_axis staleness: a fresh real reading (incl. a negative one) is NOT UNREACHABLE; a stale/missing
  # file IS. This is the empty-≠-failed invariant at the I/O layer.
  _td="$(mktemp -d)"; trap 'rm -rf "$_td"' EXIT
  printf 'IDLE\n' > "$_td/kbd"; _r="$(read_axis "$_td/kbd" 600)"; case "$_r" in IDLE|*) :;; esac
  [ "${_r%%|*}" = IDLE ] || { echo "  FAIL: read_axis fresh IDLE must return IDLE (got $_r)"; exit 1; }
  touch -d '1 hour ago' "$_td/kbd"; _r="$(read_axis "$_td/kbd" 600)"
  [ "${_r%%|*}" = UNREACHABLE ] || { echo "  FAIL: read_axis stale must return UNREACHABLE (got $_r)"; exit 1; }
  _r="$(read_axis "$_td/missing" 600)"; [ "${_r%%|*}" = UNREACHABLE ] || { echo "  FAIL: read_axis missing must return UNREACHABLE (got $_r)"; exit 1; }
  # a genuine EMPTY reading stays EMPTY (empty ≠ failed), not UNREACHABLE
  printf 'EMPTY\n' > "$_td/room"; _r="$(read_axis "$_td/room" 600)"; [ "${_r%%|*}" = EMPTY ] || { echo "  FAIL: genuine EMPTY must stay EMPTY not UNREACHABLE (got $_r)"; exit 1; }
  rm -rf "$_td"; trap - EXIT

  # 9. _probe — the active-sensing / epistemic-action primitive (review-efe-epistemic-active-sensing):
  #    a degraded axis -> a recommendation; priority kbd > room; a confident band -> none.
  _fuse IDLE OFF UNREACHABLE QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE 14            # room unreachable -> UNKNOWN
  _probe IDLE OFF UNREACHABLE QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE
  [ "$probe_sense" = room ] || { echo "  FAIL: probe should pick room (got $probe_sense)"; exit 1; }
  # γ (expected precision over policies): one load-bearing axis diffuse -> decisive probe -> HIGH
  [ "$probe_gamma" = HIGH ] || { echo "  FAIL: single-load-bearing probe γ should be HIGH (got $probe_gamma)"; exit 1; }
  _fuse UNREACHABLE OFF UNREACHABLE QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE 14     # kbd+room unreachable
  _probe UNREACHABLE OFF UNREACHABLE QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE
  [ "$probe_sense" = kbd ] || { echo "  FAIL: probe priority kbd>room (got $probe_sense)"; exit 1; }
  # γ: TWO load-bearing axes diffuse (kbd+room) -> one refresh is a partial move -> LOW
  [ "$probe_gamma" = LOW ] || { echo "  FAIL: two-load-bearing probe γ should be LOW (got $probe_gamma)"; exit 1; }
  # γ: only a WEAK-LEVER axis diffuse (light) -> probe picks light but confidence is LOW
  _probe IDLE OFF PRESENT QUIET SILENT UNREACHABLE IDLE
  [ "$probe_sense" = light ] || { echo "  FAIL: probe should pick light when only lt unreachable (got $probe_sense)"; exit 1; }
  [ "$probe_gamma" = LOW ] || { echo "  FAIL: weak-lever probe γ should be LOW (got $probe_gamma)"; exit 1; }
  _fuse IDLE OFF EMPTY QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE 14                  # genuine AWAY, no degraded axis
  _probe IDLE OFF EMPTY QUIET SILENT DARK IDLE
  [ "$probe_sense" = none ] || { echo "  FAIL: confident band needs no probe (got $probe_sense)"; exit 1; }
  _fuse IDLE OFF PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK UNKNOWN 14            # op-awake UNKNOWN only -> probe awake
  _probe IDLE OFF PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK UNKNOWN
  [ "$probe_sense" = awake ] || { echo "  FAIL: probe should pick awake when only oa unknown (got $probe_sense)"; exit 1; }

  # 10. THE NON-TRIVIAL MACHINE (von Foerster) — the --edge debounce STATE MACHINE.
  #   review-second-order-cyb-nontrivial-machine-2026-07-27. GATEs 1-9 all exercise the TRIVIAL half:
  #   _fuse/_probe/read_axis are pure input→output (state-free), fixture-swept 18 ways. But --edge (the
  #   2-consecutive debounce over STATE+PENDING, lines ~388-412) is a NON-TRIVIAL machine — its output
  #   depends on HISTORY, so no single drive can witness a transition, and until now nothing tested it.
  #   Von Foerster's point: you cannot reach a non-trivial machine's behaviour by testing it as if
  #   trivial; you must drive it through a SEQUENCE of states and observe the transitions. Do exactly
  #   that on the REAL script (subprocess, seeded axes) across onset→hold→recovery, asserting every
  #   branch: cold commit · single-flap HELD (debounce) · 2nd-sample commit (onset edge) · BOTH edges
  #   symmetric (recovery also debounced+commits) · stable-hold clears pending · state-touch fires every
  #   LIVE run. band pair DO-NOT-DISTURB↔FOCUSED is hour-independent (both are dominated by explicit
  #   attention signals — typing / awake+bright — which override the night/RESTING branch), so the
  #   sequence is deterministic at any wall-clock (verified live at hour=22).
  _eh="$(mktemp -d)"; mkdir -p "$_eh/.mesh" "$_eh/bin"
  _est="$_eh/.mesh/.interruptibility.state"; _epn="$_eh/.mesh/.interruptibility.pending"
  _ewit="$_eh/.mesh/.touch-witness"; : > "$_ewit"
  printf '#!/bin/sh\necho AWAKE\n' > "$_eh/bin/mesh-operator-awake"   # digital presence fixed AWAKE (needed for FOCUSED; harmless to DND — typing dominates)
  printf '#!/bin/sh\nprintf "x\\n" >> "%s"\ntouch "$1"\n' "$_ewit" > "$_eh/bin/mesh-state-touch"
  chmod +x "$_eh/bin/mesh-operator-awake" "$_eh/bin/mesh-state-touch"
  _pDND(){    # kbd TYPING dominates → DO-NOT-DISTURB
    printf 'TYPING\n' >"$_eh/.mesh/.kbd-activity.state"; printf 'OFF\n'   >"$_eh/.mesh/.screen-state.state"
    printf 'EMPTY\n'  >"$_eh/.mesh/.room-sense.state";   printf 'QUIET\n' >"$_eh/.mesh/.ambient-clock.state"
    printf 'SILENT\n' >"$_eh/.mesh/.activity-tempo.state";printf 'DARK\n' >"$_eh/.mesh/.light-state"; }
  _pFOC(){    # awake + bright + present → FOCUSED
    printf 'IDLE\n'   >"$_eh/.mesh/.kbd-activity.state"; printf 'BRIGHT\n' >"$_eh/.mesh/.screen-state.state"
    printf 'PRESENT\n'>"$_eh/.mesh/.room-sense.state";   printf 'QUIET\n'  >"$_eh/.mesh/.ambient-clock.state"
    printf 'RESTING\n'>"$_eh/.mesh/.activity-tempo.state";printf 'LIT\n'   >"$_eh/.mesh/.light-state"; }
  _edge(){ env -i HOME="$_eh" PATH="$_eh/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" bash "$0" --edge >/dev/null 2>&1; }
  _efail(){ echo "  FAIL: edge state-machine — $1"; rm -rf "$_eh"; exit 1; }
  # a) cold start (no STATE): commit immediately, no pending
  _pFOC; _edge
  [ "$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)" = "FOCUSED|na=|degraded=" ] || _efail "cold-start must commit FOCUSED with an empty degraded field (got '$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)')"
  [ -e "$_epn" ] && _efail "cold-start must leave no pending"
  # b) single flap toward DND: debounce HOLDS — STATE stays FOCUSED, pending armed at :1
  _pDND; _edge
  [ "$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)" = "FOCUSED|na=|degraded=" ] || _efail "single flap must NOT flip band (got STATE='$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)')"
  [ "$(cat "$_epn" 2>/dev/null)" = "DO-NOT-DISTURB|na=|degraded=:1" ] || _efail "single flap must arm pending :1 (got '$(cat "$_epn" 2>/dev/null)')"
  # c) 2nd consecutive DND: onset edge COMMITS, pending cleared
  _pDND; _edge
  [ "$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)" = "DO-NOT-DISTURB|na=|degraded=" ] || _efail "2nd consecutive sample must commit onset (got '$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)')"
  [ -e "$_epn" ] && _efail "commit must clear pending"
  # d) single flap back to FOCUSED: recovery edge is debounced TOO — STATE stays DND, pending FOCUSED:1
  _pFOC; _edge
  [ "$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)" = "DO-NOT-DISTURB|na=|degraded=" ] || _efail "recovery single flap must NOT flip (both edges symmetric) (got '$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)')"
  [ "$(cat "$_epn" 2>/dev/null)" = "FOCUSED|na=|degraded=:1" ] || _efail "recovery must arm pending FOCUSED:1 (got '$(cat "$_epn" 2>/dev/null)')"
  # e) 2nd consecutive FOCUSED: recovery edge COMMITS
  _pFOC; _edge
  [ "$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)" = "FOCUSED|na=|degraded=" ] || _efail "recovery 2nd sample must commit (got '$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)')"
  # f) stable hold (band == confirmed): pending stays clear, STATE unchanged
  _pFOC; _edge
  [ "$(cat "$_est" 2>/dev/null)" = "FOCUSED|na=|degraded=" ] || _efail "stable hold must keep committed band"
  [ -e "$_epn" ] && _efail "stable hold must not arm pending"
  # liveness: mesh-state-touch fires on EVERY live run (mtime=ran-live), not just on a value change
  [ "$(wc -l < "$_ewit")" -ge 6 ] || _efail "state-touch must fire every live run (got $(wc -l < "$_ewit") of 6)"
  rm -rf "$_eh"

  # 10b. THE ARTIFACT CARRIES THE DEGRADED LIST — gate 6d one layer down.
  #   6d asserts two UNKNOWNs differ in the in-memory `$degraded`. That proved nothing about what
  #   reaches disk: the --edge write published `$band` alone, so both fixtures produced the SAME
  #   byte-identical state file and the "visibly distinct artifacts" contract was vacated by the one
  #   line that publishes. Drive the REAL script twice from two cold homes — a clean-signal UNKNOWN
  #   (every axis a real read, ambient loud → no band matches; a refresh would not help) and a blind
  #   UNKNOWN (kbd+screen state files absent) — and assert the two ARTIFACTS differ and that the blind
  #   one NAMES its dead axes. Delete the `|degraded=` half of the record and this goes red.
  #   Both fixtures are hour-independent: light=LIT kills the night/RESTING branch at any wall-clock.
  _u_drive(){ # $1=blind|clean → echoes the committed state record from a fresh cold home
    local h; h="$(mktemp -d)"; mkdir -p "$h/.mesh" "$h/bin"
    printf '#!/bin/sh\necho AWAKE\n' > "$h/bin/mesh-operator-awake"
    printf '#!/bin/sh\ntouch "$1"\n'  > "$h/bin/mesh-state-touch"
    chmod +x "$h/bin/mesh-operator-awake" "$h/bin/mesh-state-touch"
    printf 'PRESENT\n' >"$h/.mesh/.room-sense.state";    printf 'ACTIVE\n'  >"$h/.mesh/.ambient-clock.state"
    printf 'RESTING\n' >"$h/.mesh/.activity-tempo.state"; printf 'LIT\n'    >"$h/.mesh/.light-state"
    if [ "$1" = clean ]; then   # every axis a REAL read → degraded MUST stay empty
      printf 'IDLE\n' >"$h/.mesh/.kbd-activity.state";   printf 'DIM\n' >"$h/.mesh/.screen-state.state"
    fi                          # blind: kbd + screen files simply absent → UNREACHABLE
    env -i HOME="$h" PATH="$h/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" bash "$0" --edge >/dev/null 2>&1
    cat "$h/.mesh/.interruptibility.state" 2>/dev/null; rm -rf "$h"
  }
  _u_clean="$(_u_drive clean)"; _u_blind="$(_u_drive blind)"
  [ "${_u_clean%%|*}" = UNKNOWN ] || { echo "  FAIL: clean fixture must band UNKNOWN (got '$_u_clean')"; exit 1; }
  [ "${_u_blind%%|*}" = UNKNOWN ] || { echo "  FAIL: blind fixture must band UNKNOWN (got '$_u_blind')"; exit 1; }
  [ "$_u_clean" != "$_u_blind" ] || { echo "  FAIL: blind and clean UNKNOWN published IDENTICAL artifacts ('$_u_clean') — the degraded list never reaches disk"; exit 1; }
  [ "$_u_clean" = 'UNKNOWN|na=|degraded=' ] || { echo "  FAIL: a clean UNKNOWN must publish EMPTY na= and degraded= fields (got '$_u_clean')"; exit 1; }
  # The blind fixture's tools are NOT on its PATH, so the absence oracle must return UNPROBEABLE and
  # the axes must stay UNREACHABLE: "could not ask" is not "the organ is gone", and if that ever
  # inverted, this whole blindness fixture would quietly become an absence fixture and stop testing
  # blindness at all.
  case "$_u_blind" in *'|na=|'*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: an UNPROBEABLE organ (tool not on PATH) must NOT be recorded as absent — got '$_u_blind'"; exit 1 ;; esac
  case "$_u_blind" in
    *kbd-unreachable*screen-unreachable*) : ;;
    *) echo "  FAIL: a blind UNKNOWN must NAME its dead axes on disk (got '$_u_blind')"; exit 1 ;;
  esac

  # 10. _foreclosure — ASSISTIVE-EMPOWERMENT (ESR) selection preference.
  #   The load-bearing gate is the ESR ORDERING: a reversible-private form MUST foreclose the
  #   operator's option-space LESS than an exclusive-irreversible one. Invert the table sign and this
  #   goes red. (review-info-theory-agency-assistive-operator-empowerment-2026-07-28.)
  _foreclosure tg-line          || { echo "  FAIL: tg-line must score"; exit 1; }; _fc_tg=$fc_score
  _foreclosure speaker-autoplay || { echo "  FAIL: speaker-autoplay must score"; exit 1; }; _fc_sp=$fc_score
  [ "$_fc_tg" -lt "$_fc_sp" ] || { echo "  FAIL: ESR ordering — reversible-private (tg-line=$_fc_tg) must foreclose LESS than exclusive-irreversible (speaker-autoplay=$_fc_sp)"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure tg-line;         [ "$fc_band" = LOW ]  || { echo "  FAIL: tg-line must be LOW band (got $fc_band)"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure act-third-party; [ "$fc_band" = HIGH ] || { echo "  FAIL: act-third-party must be HIGH band (got $fc_band)"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure raw 0 0 0; [ "$fc_band" = LOW ]  || { echo "  FAIL: raw 0 0 0 must be LOW (got $fc_band)"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure raw 3 3 2; [ "$fc_band" = HIGH ] || { echo "  FAIL: raw 3 3 2 must be HIGH (got $fc_band)"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure raw 5 0 0 && { echo "  FAIL: out-of-range dim must be refused"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure raw 0 0 0 +party 5 0 0 && { echo "  FAIL: out-of-range BYSTANDER dim must be refused"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure bogus-form && { echo "  FAIL: unknown form must be refused, NOT scored as 0 (silent-all-clear trap)"; exit 1; }

  # 10b. FAIR MULTI-PARTY AGGREGATION — Heitzig & Potham (arXiv:2608.08240, 2026-08-08).
  #   Until 2026-08-20 a co-present bystander was a PROSE CAVEAT that never moved the score, so an act
  #   free for the operator and irreversible for a bystander read `band=LOW` with a footnote. These
  #   gates assert the three axioms that fix it. Each has been seen RED: reverting `agg` to
  #   `$fc_score` reds (LIMITED TRADE-OFF); swapping the soft-min for a mean reds (SUM-REJECTION);
  #   dropping the `f<=0 → skip` line reds (DISEMPOWERMENT FOCUS).
  _fc_gt(){ awk -v a="$1" -v b="$2" 'BEGIN{ exit !(a > b) }'; }
  _fc_near(){ awk -v a="$1" -v b="$2" -v t="$3" 'BEGIN{ d=a-b; if(d<0)d=-d; exit !(d <= t) }'; }

  #   DISEMPOWERMENT FOCUS — an UNTOUCHED co-present party (all bystander dims 0) cannot change the
  #   verdict; the single-party path must reduce EXACTLY to the old number.
  _foreclosure tg-line;        _fc_a="$fc_agg"; _fc_b="$fc_band"
  _foreclosure tg-line +party; [ "$fc_band" = "$_fc_b" ] || { echo "  FAIL disempowerment-focus: an UNAFFECTED bystander changed the band ($_fc_b -> $fc_band)"; exit 1; }
  _fc_near "$fc_agg" "$_fc_a" 0.05 || { echo "  FAIL disempowerment-focus: an UNAFFECTED bystander moved the aggregate ($_fc_a -> $fc_agg)"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure speaker-autoplay; _fc_a="$fc_agg"
  _fc_near "$_fc_a" "$fc_score" 0.05 || { echo "  FAIL: with no party the aggregate MUST equal the operator score ($fc_score vs $_fc_a) — the reduction property"; exit 1; }

  #   LIMITED TRADE-OFF (their Cor. 4.1) — an act FREE for the operator and irreversible for the
  #   bystander must NOT band LOW. This is the exact case the prose caveat let through.
  _foreclosure raw 0 0 0 +party 3 3 3 || { echo "  FAIL: raw+party must score"; exit 1; }
  [ "$fc_band" = HIGH ] || { echo "  FAIL limited-trade-off: operator-free / bystander-destroying act banded $fc_band (agg=$fc_agg) — the bystander is back to being a footnote"; exit 1; }
  #   SUM-REJECTION — a utilitarian sum/mean over the two parties would call that act 4.5/9 = MED
  #   (the utility-monster the paper's axioms rule out). The soft-min must stay above the MED cut.
  _fc_gt "$fc_agg" 5 || { echo "  FAIL sum-rejection: aggregate $fc_agg is at or below the mean of the two parties — an averaging aggregator has crept back in"; exit 1; }
  #   ...and no amount of operator empowerment buys it back: worsening ONLY the operator side can
  #   never IMPROVE the aggregate.
  _fc_c="$fc_agg"; _foreclosure raw 3 3 3 +party 3 3 3
  _fc_gt "$_fc_c" "$fc_agg" && { echo "  FAIL limited-trade-off: aggregate IMPROVED ($_fc_c -> $fc_agg) when the operator's own foreclosure rose — the aggregator is compensating"; exit 1; }

  #   PIGOU-DALTON (inequality aversion) — same TOTAL foreclosure, split evenly, must aggregate BETTER
  #   than concentrated on one party. A sum cannot tell these apart; that is the point.
  _foreclosure raw 0 0 0 +party 3 3 0; _fc_uneq="$fc_agg"   # (0,6)
  _foreclosure raw 1 1 1 +party 1 1 1; _fc_eq="$fc_agg"     # (3,3), same total
  _fc_gt "$_fc_uneq" "$_fc_eq" || { echo "  FAIL pigou-dalton: concentrated harm (0,6)=$_fc_uneq must aggregate WORSE than the even split (3,3)=$_fc_eq"; exit 1; }

  #   XI is the inequality-aversion knob and must BITE: as xi grows the aggregate converges on the
  #   worst-off party (exact min). A hardcoded xi, or dropping the /xi normalisation, reds this.
  ( MESH_FC_XI=16; _foreclosure raw 1 1 1 +party 1 1 1
    _fc_near "$fc_agg" 3 0.25 || { echo "  FAIL xi: at xi=16 the aggregate must converge on the worst-off party (3.0), got $fc_agg"; exit 1; } ) || exit 1
  ( MESH_FC_XI=0.5; _foreclosure raw 1 1 1 +party 1 1 1
    _fc_gt "$fc_agg" 4.5 || { echo "  FAIL xi: at xi=0.5 (weak aversion) the aggregate must sit ABOVE the xi=1 value 4.0, got $fc_agg"; exit 1; } ) || exit 1

  #   The caveat must carry the NUMBER, not prose — a safety knob named only in words is the failure
  #   this whole block exists to close.
  _foreclosure act-third-party +party
  case "$fc_caveat" in *bystander-foreclosure=*/9*) : ;;
    *) echo "  FAIL: the multi-party caveat must quote the bystander's SCORE, not just prose (got '$fc_caveat')"; exit 1 ;; esac
  [ -n "$fc_bscore" ] || { echo "  FAIL: +party must set fc_bscore"; exit 1; }
  _foreclosure act-third-party
  [ -z "$fc_caveat" ] || { echo "  FAIL: no party → no caveat (got '$fc_caveat')"; exit 1; }
  [ -z "$fc_bscore" ] || { echo "  FAIL: no party → no bystander score (got '$fc_bscore')"; exit 1; }

  # VOCABULARY COVERAGE — every band mesh-light can EMIT must survive light_vocab as ITSELF. The
  # guard exists to stop non-levels ("OFFLINE <ts>", error prose) masquerading as readings; when the
  # vocabulary lags the emitter it does the opposite and ERASES a real one. Founding case 2026-08-18:
  # mesh-light emits SIX bands over TWO scales (lux DARK|DIM|MODERATE|LIT|BRIGHT, webcam-coarse
  # DARK|DIM|TWILIGHT|LIT); TWILIGHT landed 2026-07-02 (8c96cb6) and was missing here for 47 days, so
  # a live mid-luma read of the room came back UNREACHABLE. Re-derived from mesh-light's SOURCE every
  # run — a hardcoded band list would rot on the next band exactly as this one did.
  _ml="$(command -v mesh-light 2>/dev/null)"
  if [ -n "$_ml" ]; then
    _bands="$({ grep -oE 'lvl = "[A-Z]+"' "$_ml" | grep -oE '[A-Z]{3,}'
                grep -oE 'echo [A-Z]{3,9};'  "$_ml" | grep -oE '[A-Z]{3,}'; } | sort -u)"
    # A loop over an empty list asserts nothing: fail LOUD if the extraction stops matching.
    _nb="$(printf '%s\n' "$_bands" | grep -c .)"
    [ "$_nb" -ge 5 ] || { echo "  FAIL vocab-coverage: band extraction from $_ml found only $_nb level(s) — the emit sites moved, so this gate is vacuous; re-derive it"; exit 1; }
    for _b in $_bands; do
      [ "$(light_vocab "$_b")" = "$_b" ] || { echo "  FAIL vocab-coverage: mesh-light emits the band $_b but light_vocab erases it to $(light_vocab "$_b") — the anti-masquerade guard is deleting a REAL reading"; exit 1; }
    done
    # ...and the guard must still DO its job: non-levels stay UNREACHABLE, or the gate above could be
    # satisfied by deleting the case altogether.
    for _n in OFFLINE '' 'OFFLINE 2026-08-18T00:00:00Z' covered no-frame; do
      [ "$(light_vocab "$_n")" = UNREACHABLE ] || { echo "  FAIL vocab-coverage: non-level '$_n' must collapse to UNREACHABLE (got $(light_vocab "$_n"))"; exit 1; }
    done
  fi

  # ---- 12. ORGAN-ABSENCE: an organ this body does not have must not delete the sense ----------
  # The bug this gate locks out: kbd/screen UNREACHABLE made _fuse a CONSTANT. Assert it with the
  # SWEEP that found it, not with one hand-picked row — a single fixture cannot show "no input
  # reaches any other band", which is the whole claim. Both arms run: the absent arm must reach
  # more than one band, and the UNREACHABLE arm must STILL collapse to exactly one (the honest
  # withholding is not being deleted, it is being scoped to the case it was written for).
  _sweep(){ # $1=kbd $2=screen → sorted unique bands over the remaining axis space
    local _k="$1" _s="$2" _r _a _t _l _o _h _seen=""
    for _r in PRESENT EMPTY UNCERTAIN UNREACHABLE; do
     for _a in QUIET SILENT MODERATE LOUD UNREACHABLE; do
      for _t in SILENT RESTING STILL ACTIVE DEGRADED UNREACHABLE; do
       for _l in DARK DIM TWILIGHT MODERATE LIT BRIGHT UNREACHABLE; do
        for _o in AWAKE RECENT IDLE ASLEEP UNKNOWN; do
         for _h in 0 8 14 23; do
           _fuse "$_k" "$_s" "$_r" "$_a" "$_t" "$_l" "$_o" "$_h"
           case " $_seen " in *" $band "*) ;; *) _seen="$_seen $band" ;; esac
         done; done; done; done; done; done
    printf '%s' "$_seen" | tr ' ' '\n' | grep -c . 
  }
  _n_abs="$(_sweep ABSENT ABSENT)"
  _n_unr="$(_sweep UNREACHABLE UNREACHABLE)"
  _n_ctl="$(_sweep IDLE OFF)"
  [ "$_n_unr" -eq 1 ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12a: kbd+screen UNREACHABLE must still collapse to exactly ONE band (the honest withholding) — got $_n_unr. Scoping absence must not weaken the degraded case."; exit 1; }
  [ "$_n_abs" -ge 3 ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12b: kbd+screen ABSENT must reach >=3 bands — got $_n_abs. An organ this node cannot have is deleting the sense; that is the 240-run constant this gate exists to stop."; exit 1; }
  [ "$_n_ctl" -ge "$_n_abs" ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12c: the ABSENT arm ($_n_abs) reaches MORE bands than the fully-sensed control ($_n_ctl) — absence must never buy MORE resolution than a real read."; exit 1; }
  # 12d. the two reasons stay on SEPARATE fields: absent never leaks into degraded and vice versa.
  _fuse ABSENT ABSENT PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK AWAKE 14
  [ "$band" = AVAILABLE ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12d: present+quiet+idle with kbd ABSENT must reach AVAILABLE (got $band: $reason)"; exit 1; }
  [ "$absent" = "kbd,screen" ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12d: absent list must be 'kbd,screen' (got '$absent')"; exit 1; }
  [ -z "$degraded" ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12d: an ABSENT axis must NOT enter the degraded list (got '$degraded') — that collapse is the bug"; exit 1; }
  case "$signals" in *"n/a=kbd,screen"*) ;; *) echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12d: an all-clear on a narrowed basis must NAME the basis in signals (got: $signals)"; exit 1 ;; esac
  # 12e. ...and an UNREACHABLE kbd on the SAME row is still withheld (the guard kept its teeth).
  _fuse UNREACHABLE UNREACHABLE PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK AWAKE 14
  [ "$band" = UNKNOWN ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12e: the same row with kbd UNREACHABLE must stay withheld (got $band)"; exit 1; }
  [ -z "$absent" ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12e: an UNREACHABLE axis must not be reported as absent (got '$absent')"; exit 1; }
  # 12f. _probe never nominates an organ that does not exist — there is no refresh that grows one.
  _probe ABSENT ABSENT PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK AWAKE
  [ "$probe_sense" != kbd ] && [ "$probe_sense" != screen ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12f: _probe nominated an ABSENT organ ($probe_sense) — a refresh cannot produce a sense this body lacks"; exit 1; }
  # 12g. the ABSENCE ORACLE itself, incl. reflex-health's test-forgery + unprobeable refusals.
  [ "$(_absent_verdict 1 0 2 0)" = ABSENT ]      || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12g: rc=2 + no artifact before or after must be ABSENT"; exit 1; }
  [ "$(_absent_verdict 1 0 2 1)" = FORGED ]      || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12g: a --test that CREATES the artifact must be refused the absence verdict (TEST-FORGED)"; exit 1; }
  [ "$(_absent_verdict 1 1 2 1)" = PRESENT ]     || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12g: an existing artifact is a corpse, not an absent organ"; exit 1; }
  [ "$(_absent_verdict 1 0 0 0)" = PRESENT ]     || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12g: rc=0 means the organ can produce — never ABSENT"; exit 1; }
  [ "$(_absent_verdict 1 0 1 0)" = PRESENT ]     || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12g: rc=1 is a failing organ, not a missing one"; exit 1; }
  [ "$(_absent_verdict 0 0 9 0)" = UNPROBEABLE ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12g: no binary to ask ⇒ 'could not ask' is not 'the organ is gone'"; exit 1; }
  # 12h. _all_dark still fires when every axis is dark for the NEW reason (exit 2 must not go away).
  _all_dark ABSENT ABSENT ABSENT QUIET SILENT DARK UNKNOWN || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12h: all axes ABSENT must still be all-dark (exit 2) — a more precise reason is not more information"; exit 1; }
  _all_dark ABSENT ABSENT PRESENT QUIET SILENT DARK UNKNOWN && { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12h: a live room axis must defeat all-dark"; exit 1; } || true
  # 12i. the WIRE: the record keeps `na=` BETWEEN band and degraded, so an un-updated reader using
  # `#*|degraded=` still extracts the degraded csv alone (a missed reader degrades to silence).
  _rec="BAND|na=kbd,screen|degraded=room-unreachable"
  [ "${_rec%%|*}" = BAND ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12i: band extraction broke"; exit 1; }
  [ "${_rec#*|degraded=}" = "room-unreachable" ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12i: the legacy degraded= extraction must still yield the degraded csv ALONE (got '${_rec#*|degraded=}') — field order is what makes a missed reader silent instead of wrong"; exit 1; }
  _na="${_rec#*|na=}"; _na="${_na%%|*}"
  [ "$_na" = "kbd,screen" ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12i: na= extraction must yield the absent csv (got '$_na')"; exit 1; }

  # 12j. END-TO-END — the assertions above all live at the _fuse/_absent_verdict layer, and source
  # text is never behaviour. Drive the REAL script from a cold home whose kbd/screen organs are on
  # PATH and honestly n/a (--test exits 2, writes nothing) and assert what reaches DISK. Three arms
  # from ONE fixture generator so the absence arm cannot pass by reading another arm's artifact:
  #   absent  → the band escapes UNKNOWN and the record NAMES the narrowed basis
  #   forged  → the same organs, but --test WRITES the artifact: absence REFUSED, axis stays dark
  #   missing → the organs are not on PATH at all: UNPROBEABLE, absence refused
  _oa_drive(){ # $1=absent|forged|missing → committed record from a fresh cold home
    local h; h="$(mktemp -d)"; mkdir -p "$h/.mesh" "$h/bin"
    printf '#!/bin/sh\necho AWAKE\n' > "$h/bin/mesh-operator-awake"
    printf '#!/bin/sh\ntouch "$1"\n'  > "$h/bin/mesh-state-touch"
    chmod +x "$h/bin/mesh-operator-awake" "$h/bin/mesh-state-touch"
    # PRESENT + QUIET + operator AWAKE = the AVAILABLE row, blocked today only by the kbd axis.
    printf 'PRESENT\n' >"$h/.mesh/.room-sense.state";     printf 'QUIET\n' >"$h/.mesh/.ambient-clock.state"
    printf 'SILENT\n'  >"$h/.mesh/.activity-tempo.state"; printf 'LIT\n'   >"$h/.mesh/.light-state"
    case "$1" in
      absent) printf '#!/bin/sh\nexit 2\n' > "$h/bin/mesh-kbd-activity"
              printf '#!/bin/sh\nexit 2\n' > "$h/bin/mesh-screen-state"
              chmod +x "$h/bin/mesh-kbd-activity" "$h/bin/mesh-screen-state" ;;
      forged) printf '#!/bin/sh\nprintf IDLE >"$HOME/.mesh/.kbd-activity.state"\nexit 2\n' > "$h/bin/mesh-kbd-activity"
              printf '#!/bin/sh\nprintf DIM >"$HOME/.mesh/.screen-state.state"\nexit 2\n'  > "$h/bin/mesh-screen-state"
              chmod +x "$h/bin/mesh-kbd-activity" "$h/bin/mesh-screen-state" ;;
      missing) : ;;
    esac
    env -i HOME="$h" PATH="$h/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" bash "$0" --edge >/dev/null 2>&1
    cat "$h/.mesh/.interruptibility.state" 2>/dev/null; rm -rf "$h"
  }
  _oa_abs="$(_oa_drive absent)"; _oa_frg="$(_oa_drive forged)"; _oa_mis="$(_oa_drive missing)"
  case "$_oa_abs" in
    AVAILABLE'|na=kbd,screen|degraded='*) : ;;
    *) echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12j: a body whose kbd+screen organs honestly exit 2 must publish an AVAILABLE band naming its narrowed basis — got '$_oa_abs'. This is the 240-run constant; if it reads UNKNOWN the promotion never reached the live path."; exit 1 ;;
  esac
  case "$_oa_frg" in
    *'|na=|'*) : ;;
    *) echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12j: a --test that WRITES the artifact must be refused the absence verdict on the LIVE path too — got '$_oa_frg'"; exit 1 ;;
  esac
  case "$_oa_mis" in
    *'|na=|'*) : ;;
    *) echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12j: an organ not on PATH is UNPROBEABLE, never absent — got '$_oa_mis'"; exit 1 ;;
  esac
  [ "$_oa_abs" != "$_oa_frg" ] || { echo "  FAIL organ-absence 12j: the absent and forged arms published IDENTICAL artifacts — the forgery refusal is invisible on disk"; exit 1; }

  echo "smoke-test: ok (18 fusion + honest-degraded + staleness + 4 epistemic-probe + 3 probe-γ-confidence + real all-dark exit-2 run + 6-step edge state-machine + 10 foreclosure/ESR + 10b fair-multi-party (disempowerment-focus/limited-trade-off/sum-rejection/pigou-dalton/xi) + 11 vocab-coverage + 12 organ-absence [sweep: UNREACHABLE arm collapses to 1 band, ABSENT arm reaches >=3, control >= absent, absent/degraded stay separate fields, withholding keeps its teeth on UNREACHABLE, probe never nominates an absent organ, oracle absent/forged/corpse/rc0/rc1/unprobeable, all-dark survives, wire field order, END-TO-END absent/forged/unprobeable arms differ on disk])"; exit 0
fi

MODE=oneshot; [ "${1:-}" = --edge ] && MODE=edge; [ "${1:-}" = --json ] && MODE=json; [ "${1:-}" = --probe ] && MODE=probe
TS="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"; HOUR="$(date +%H)"

# --- gather axes from cached reflex STATE artifacts (cheap; each carries its own freshness) ---
kbd="$(read_axis "$MESH/.kbd-activity.state" "$KBD_STALE")";   kbd="${kbd%%|*}"
scr="$(read_axis "$MESH/.screen-state.state" "$SCREEN_STALE")"; scr="${scr%%|*}"
# Promote UNREACHABLE → ABSENT where the ORGAN ITSELF declares n/a (its --test exits 2 and the dry
# run wrote nothing). Only these two axes are promoted: they are the ones whose absence is a
# permanent property of a body (a node with no keyboard and no screen session), while room/ambient/
# tempo/light organs exist here and an outage there is a genuine degradation. Cached 6h, so the two
# --test invocations cost nothing on the /12 cron path.
[ "$kbd" = UNREACHABLE ] && organ_absent mesh-kbd-activity "$MESH/.kbd-activity.state" && kbd=ABSENT
[ "$scr" = UNREACHABLE ] && organ_absent mesh-screen-state "$MESH/.screen-state.state" && scr=ABSENT
room="$(read_axis "$MESH/.room-sense.state" "$ROOM_STALE")";    room="${room%%|*}"
amb="$(read_axis "$MESH/.ambient-clock.state" "$AMBIENT_STALE")"; amb="${amb%%|*}"
tmp="$(read_axis "$MESH/.activity-tempo.state" "$TEMPO_STALE")"; tmp="${tmp%%|*}"
lt="$(read_axis "$MESH/.light-state" "$LIGHT_STALE")";          lt="${lt%%|*}"
# light-state emits "OFFLINE <ts>" when the phone-light organ is down (and other non-level prose on
# error) — those are an UNREACHABLE light axis, NOT a brightness level. Collapse anything outside the
# known level vocabulary to UNREACHABLE so it can never masquerade as a real DARK/LIT reading.
# TWILIGHT is part of that vocabulary (webcam-coarse band, 80-109 mean luma, landed 2026-07-02) and
# was missing here for 47 days: a live mid-luma read collapsed to UNREACHABLE, i.e. the guard meant to
# stop non-levels masquerading as readings was instead erasing a real one.
lt="$(light_vocab "$lt")"

# --- digital presence (live, cheap — reads a log; ORTHOGONAL to every physical sense) ---
oa="UNKNOWN"
if command -v mesh-operator-awake >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  case "$(timeout 8 mesh-operator-awake 2>/dev/null)" in
    *AWAKE*)  oa="AWAKE"  ;;
    *RECENT*) oa="RECENT" ;;
    *IDLE*)   oa="IDLE"   ;;
    *)        oa="UNKNOWN" ;;
  esac
fi

# --- honest exit 2: every presence/attention axis dark (cannot assess at all) ---
if _all_dark "$kbd" "$scr" "$room" "$amb" "$tmp" "$lt" "$oa"; then
  echo "interruptibility: all presence/attention axes unreachable (kbd=$kbd screen=$scr room=$room awake=$oa) — cannot assess" >&2
  exit 2
fi

_fuse "$kbd" "$scr" "$room" "$amb" "$tmp" "$lt" "$oa" "$HOUR"

if [ "$MODE" = probe ]; then
  # ACTIVE SENSING / EPISTEMIC ACTION (review-efe-epistemic-active-sensing-2026-07-04): on an
  # UNKNOWN/degraded band, nominate the cheapest disambiguating sense (highest expected info-gain per
  # cost). Recommend only — never auto-dispatch (conservative-actuator doctrine).
  _probe "$kbd" "$scr" "$room" "$amb" "$tmp" "$lt" "$oa"
  if [ "$probe_sense" = none ] && [ -n "$absent" ]; then
    # An absent organ is never nominated: there is no refresh that produces a sense this body lacks.
    # Saying "a refresh would not help" WITHOUT naming why would read as "the world is ambiguous",
    # which is the same collapse in the recommendation layer.
    printf '[interruptibility:probe] none — band=%s, no DEGRADED axis; %s structurally absent on this node (no organ to refresh — the band rests on the remaining axes and says so)\n' "$band" "$absent"
  elif [ "$probe_sense" = none ]; then
    printf '[interruptibility:probe] none — band=%s, no degraded axis (UNKNOWN here is mixed real signals, not unreachable — a refresh would not help)\n' "$band"
  else
    printf '[interruptibility:probe] %s — run \`%s\` | %s · confidence=%s γ (%s)\n' \
      "$probe_sense" "$probe_cmd" "$probe_reason" "$probe_gamma" "$probe_gamma_reason"
  fi
  exit 0
fi

emit_text(){ printf '[interruptibility] %s — %s | %s\n' "$band" "$reason" "$signals"; }
emit_json(){
  local dgr abs; [ -z "$degraded" ] && dgr='""' || dgr="\"$degraded\""
  [ -z "$absent" ] && abs='""' || abs="\"$absent\""
  printf '{"band":"%s","degraded":%s,"absent":%s,"reason":"%s","signals":"%s","ts":"%s"}\n' \
    "$band" "$dgr" "$abs" "$reason" "$signals" "$TS"
}

if [ "$MODE" = json ]; then emit_json; exit 0; fi

if [ "$MODE" = edge ]; then
  # 2-consecutive debounce (mirrors mesh-activity-tempo): a single flapping sample does not flip the
  # published band. LIVENESS: touch STATE every LIVE run so a long-stable-but-LIVE band (re-confirmed
  # every cycle) never decays to a FALSE STALE — staleness means "reflex STOPPED", never "value held".
  # THE PUBLISHED RECORD IS band + degraded, NOT the band alone. The header contract above (and
  # gate 6c/6d) says a withheld all-clear and a genuine one are "visibly distinct artifacts" — but
  # that distinction lived only in `$degraded`, an in-memory variable this write DROPPED. The durable
  # artifact carried the bare word, so the one consumer that exists (mesh-sensorium's COORDINATION
  # row → the senses pane) could not tell UNKNOWN-because-the-world-is-ambiguous (a real diffuse
  # posterior; a refresh would not help) from UNKNOWN-because-two-of-my-axes-are-dead (blind; the
  # organ is the fix). On THIS node that is not hypothetical: kbd+screen are structurally unreachable,
  # so every one of 145 consecutive runs published the same bare UNKNOWN, and reflex-health could only
  # report it as a value-frozen label — the blindness itself was nowhere on disk. The gate asserted the
  # contract at the _fuse layer and the write vacated it one line later (source text is never
  # behaviour). Record shape: `<BAND>|degraded=<csv>` — always both fields, so a reader never has to
  # guess whether an absent payload means "clean" or "old writer"; `degraded=` empty IS the clean claim.
  # Record shape: `<BAND>|na=<csv>|degraded=<csv>` — THREE fields now, and the order is load-bearing.
  # The existing reader (mesh-sensorium) takes the band as `%%|*` and the degraded csv as
  # `#*|degraded=`, so putting `na=` BETWEEN them leaves both of those extractions exactly right on
  # an un-updated reader (it renders the blindness clause it always did and simply does not mention
  # the n/a set) — appending it after `degraded=` instead would have swallowed it into that clause.
  # sensorium is updated in the same commit to render it; the ordering is what makes a MISSED reader
  # degrade to silence rather than to a wrong string.
  record="$band|na=${absent}|degraded=${degraded}"
  confirmed="$(cat "$STATE" 2>/dev/null || true)"
  pending_line="$(cat "$PENDING" 2>/dev/null || true)"
  # split at the LAST colon: the record half carries no colon today (band names + degraded tokens are
  # hyphen/comma only), but %%:* would silently truncate the record the day one does.
  pending="${pending_line%:*}"; pcount="${pending_line##*:}"; pcount="${pcount:-0}"
  if [ -z "$confirmed" ]; then
    printf '%s\n' "$record" > "$STATE"; rm -f "$PENDING"
  elif [ "$record" = "$confirmed" ]; then
    rm -f "$PENDING"
  elif [ "$record" = "$pending" ]; then
    pcount=$((pcount + 1))
    if [ "$pcount" -ge 2 ]; then
      printf '%s\n' "$record" > "$STATE"; rm -f "$PENDING"
      emit_text
    else
      printf '%s:%d\n' "$record" "$pcount" > "$PENDING"
    fi
  else
    printf '%s:1\n' "$record" > "$PENDING"
  fi
  # touch-state-every-LIVE-run (shared primitive, never a bare touch — chat-review/state-touch-adoption).
  mesh-state-touch "$STATE"
  exit 0
fi

emit_text
